Reticulation of chiral 1,1'-biphenol-based imidodiphosphoric acid (IDP) into two Dy metal-organic frameworks (MOFs) allows controlling conformations and local chiral microenvironments of the organocatalyst. The MOF containing the 4-connected IDPs that takes a relative less compact shape can be an efficient and recyclable heterogeneous Brønsted acid catalyst to promote the challenging asymmetric $^{O,O}$ -acetalization of diol and aldehyde with up to $96\%$ ee.
